{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sauvc/rulebook/pulls/25","id":4811777849,"node_id":"PR_kwDOA9B6c88AAAABHs3nOQ","html_url":"https://github.com/sauvc/rulebook/pull/25","diff_url":"https://github.com/sauvc/rulebook/pull/25.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/sauvc/rulebook/pull/25.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sauvc/rulebook/issues/25","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sauvc/rulebook/pulls/25/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sauvc/rulebook/pulls/25/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sauvc/rulebook/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sauvc/rulebook/issues/25/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sauvc/rulebook/statuses/aa08ca07b1dd9f3a28b75213beb7502305c252c2","number":25,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Draft 2027 rulebook from the 2025 edition","user":{"login":"notthetup","id":553140,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MzE0MA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/553140?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/notthetup","html_url":"https://github.com/notthetup","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/notthetup/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/notthetup/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/notthetup/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/notthetup/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/notthetup/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/notthetup/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/notthetup/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/notthetup/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/notthetup/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This resets the rulebook to the 2025 edition and adds the rule changes from the technical meeting on 8 October 2026. The 2026 edition was a one-off for the Sanya venue, so 2027 builds on 2025.\n\nChanges from 2025:\n\n- The video must be 40 to 45 seconds long. It must show at least 20 seconds underwater, with the AUV diving, swimming straight, turning 180° clockwise and swimming back.\n- The video must show the kill switch operated underwater and the thrusters stopping at once. The AUV must use the same kill switch at the competition, and a diver must find it easy to reach and operate.\n- The judges check each video for authenticity. Teams may improve the AUV after the video, but must not change it significantly or modify the kill switch.\n- The judges can disallow any team whose AUV breaks the safety rules.\n- Parts that extend and retract during a run count towards weight but not size.\n- New surfacing square bonus. If the AUV has completed Navigation and surfaces inside a 200×200cm square next to the qualification gates without touching it, the team gets 20 points on top of the usual 5 point surfacing bonus. Touching the square counts as a normal surface.\n- New arena diagram. The flares are on the left side, the operating area is wider, and the Surfacing Square sits next to the qualification gates.\n- New Surfacing Square diagram. The prop table now says the markers are blue and hang about 30cm below the frame.\n- Every example now shows both surfacing bonuses. Examples 8 to 10 are new and cover the square. Example 4 had the wrong total in 2025. It said 105, the real total is 85.\n- Versions now follow YYYY.MAJOR.PATCH, starting at 2027.1.1. The README explains the scheme.\n- Fixed the broken task links in the Tasks list and a handful of typos.\n\nStill to do before this leaves draft:\n\n- [x] Video deadline, set to 20th December, 2026\n- [x] New arena diagram with flares on the left side, a wider operating area and the surfacing square\n- [x] Surfacing square illustration\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-10T14:07:05Z","updated_at":"2026-10-26T02:36:26Z"